    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d225">

                <pb facs="0170" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">715.1715/1426: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Representative of the President</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Corrigan</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-05-19T11:00:00-05:00">May 19, 1939—11
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 4:04 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>53. Reference the Legation’s despatch No. 741, May 6,<anchor n="30"
                        xml:id="d225-f1"/> the Venezuelan member, after consultation with his
                    Government, approves sending Ocheltree to Tegucigalpa on a technical errand for
                    the Mediation Commission to familiarize Honduran Government officials with
                    geographic studies now in the hands of the Permanent Secretariat at <pb
                        facs="0171" n="163" xml:id="pg163"/> San José. President of the Commission
                    has been informed through Ocheltree.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Corrigan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
